{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fleeting-choosey-dore","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n`make lint` deterministically prints: `WARN audit: zizmor is running in offline mode by default; some audits and auto-fixes will not be available.` The gate still exits successfully, so contributors can report a clean lint run while the tool says part of its audit surface is unavailable. A tracker search for `zizmor offline mode` found no open bug owning the warning. Discovered while verifying `treelike-unamusing-grosbeak`.\n\n## Reproduction\nFrom a provisioned checkout, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and inspect the zizmor step.\n\n## Plan\nUse `rebar-debug` to identify exactly which audits are disabled offline, whether Gerrit CI has network/capabilities to run them, and whether the current invocation is deliberate. If changing online/offline policy affects portability, network access, or CI behavior, return an evidence-backed decision brief rather than silently choosing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Root cause and the exact unavailable audit capabilities are proven against the pinned zizmor version.\n- [ ] Local/no-network and Gerrit CI behavior are both evaluated.\n- [ ] The warning is eliminated by a reviewed policy or explicitly documented/suppressed only if the warning is proven intentional and coverage-equivalent safeguards are cited.\n- [ ] `make lint` and relevant workflow gates remain green.","id":"7a03-74f2-e812-4104","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["warning","ci","security","zizmor"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"make lint runs zizmor offline and leaves online audits unavailable"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786922832417096001,"uuid":"8d85026b-c957-4de3-935a-fe023efb5c37"}